Eidolos, illiterate genoless polyless lawful female human Wizard

For a while now I've wanted to do an illiterate wizard. Well, now I've
done one! It took 5h 56m 43s and 32727 turns. I found no bones piles,
and spent exactly five wishes. The first wish below was pre-castle,
gotten by dipping into a fountain (thanks LittleWhiteMouse for
reminding me about converting a sink). Notice the lack of armor
wishes. :) I'm of the opinion that AC is overrated. This game did curb
that opinion a bit.. minotaurs are nasty with AC -10.

T12826:1h 53m 12s: blessed fixed greased ring of conflict
T17311:2h 47m 35s: blessed fixed greased Platinum Yendorian Express
Card
T17313:2h 48m 14s: blessed fixed greased Orb of Fate
T32076:5h 40m 44s: blessed fixed greased ring of levitation
T32326:5h 47m: blessed fixed greased wand of teleportation

My starting equipment was:

two ?oID -- sold
?oTele -- sold
spellbook of cure blindness -- never casted
spellbook of force bolt -- casted very rarely (really only in the wiz
quest against eels)
!oInvis -- diluted
!oLev -- diluted
!oOD -- diluted
=oFireRes -- never worn, probably sold
=oSeeInvis -- worn only at the castle, but could've used towel +
telepathy
/oSleep -- broken in the mines to save myself from a gnome and dwarf
-- funny story here, I forgot I was human (I almost exclusively play
elven wizards) and thus not intrinsically sleep resistant. But it
worked out okay.

Just goes to show you that starting equipment is not as important as
the start scummers would have you believe..

The early game was pretty standard. I went directly to Minetown in the
beginning, hoping for a magic lamp (to no avail). The equipment I
found on the way was nice: +0 dwarvish mithril, +0 dwarvish iron helm,
+2 iron shoes (all of which I wore to the high altar). Thankfully the
altar was coaligned, so I quickly got +0 Magicbane (which I used there
on out). Other than that, Minetown didn't have much except a can of
grease (which is more useful than you might think for illits.. damn
rust traps and rust monsters).

Then I went to Sokoban. On the first level I killed a black unicorn
(AC -2, HP 46) in straight melee which I thought was pretty good
(early). As usual, I hoped for a bag of holding, but instead I got the
reflection. Though that probably ended up saving my character when I
met a black dragon later. I also had 18 strength by the time I left
Sokoban, thanks in part to two tins of spinach.

Descending, I found the big room. I was way ill-equipped to deal with
it, so I goofed around above it. I gathered all the scrolls and
spellbooks to sell them, getting a few points of protection. In
Minetown I come across a pack of ogres, one of which read a cursed
scroll of create monster. I had a very difficult time dealing with all
the monsters: two gremlins during the gremlin-steal-intrinsic time,
though luckily I didn't lose either pois or cold, a raven who kept
blinding me, a pack of coyotes who were blocking the bottleneck, a
tiger, a red naga who mercilessly didn't really breathe flame until
things were settled down, and a few more. A few close calls, but
eventually (thanks to royal jelly's healing properties) I survived and
eventually got low enough HP to pray for a heal. I also went down to
grab the luckstone. On the way I picked up a pair of leather gloves
from a group of soldiers. I also killed the first leocrotta of the
game, which is always a good feeling. :) Those bastards are hard! In
Mine's
End (the Catacombs), I identified scroll of scare monster. Stupidly by
picking it up and dropping it until it disintegrated. Now I know to
just wait on each scroll for a monster to come attack me.

Following the suggestion of stumbly, I blessed my touchstone for two
reasons: one, to sell identified gems to shopkeepers for prot gold;
and two, to throw at unicorns to max my luck. After getting Magicbane
I avoided sacrificing at all, because I didn't want another artifact.
I planned on wishing (and later did) for the PYEC at the Castle.
Illits don't get any other charging. So the PYEC is like a free wish,
plus a chance to get one or two more wishes. This is because
nontourist PYEC charging is effectively uncursed ?oC, which sets the
wand of wishing to 1:(1d3). Sadly the gray unicorn I saw in Mine's End
hit a polytrap. I didn't end up maxing my luck until I was in the
Valley and finally met a gray unicorn.

At this point I began dipping into all the fountains. Got a wish,
spent it on a ring of conflict. Not only will it easily get me past
the big room, but it's also a decent way to take out the Castle (I
hadn't at this point found an instrument). Conflict is really one of
the best items in the game.

So I got past the big room. I found on the ground a pair of gauntlets
of power, an excellent item for any illiterate character. In a shop I
found a +0 helm of brilliance. It kinda sucks to leave behind a HoB on
a wiz, but it wouldn't have helped much at all, since I wasn't
casting. Descending further I found a general store with two huge
items: a bugle (I *love* castle instruments) and a bag of holding
(..but not as much as I love freedom from inv twiddling). So there was
really nothing stopping me from plummeting to the castle, which I did,
as soon as I went back up and gathered the swag from all my stashes.
On dlvl 17 I got a cockatrice corpse, so I stopped running around and
started digging.

Medusa was the titan variant; stoned him. Made it to the castle. No
purple liches, but there was a minotaur in the left-side maze; stoned
him. The castle was easy as usual; drawbridged everything to death.
Got to the wand, wished up a PYEC first; worked (which meant I
probably didn't dig past any major bones files). Wand turned out to be
0:1, ugh. Recharged (which I later discovered put it at 1:2), tried
wishing for the Orb of Fate; worked. Half physical damage,
levelporting, portal detection, and luckstone all in one eight ton
sphere. That was it for wishing. Down to the Valley to get XL 17 for
the Quest and for TC.

I was surprised at how well +0 Magicbane handled the denizens of the
Valley. I guess it's partly the special effects, and partly the 25
strength. I got up to level 17 and went to do the Quest. In the Quest
I found help unlooked for: a magic harp. Suddenly it clicked; what an
amazing item in conjunction with the PYEC. Now I had a viable solution
for minotaurs, disenchanters, and summon storms. So next time I try
illit that'll probably be something I wish for. Anyway, I got the Eye,
no problem. I also found my first usable scroll of scare monster. I
later blessed it, but I never ended up using it. I also cleaned out
the Minetown shks (sans Izchak, of course) with a cockatrice and
conflict. That got me a bunch of protection. Then I did the same trick
with the priest so I could get more prot later. After all this, the
bore of Gehennom finally commenced.

Using my gold I bought a bunch of clairvoyance. I levelported to the
first level Vlad's could appear on and started descending. Nothing
really noteworthy in all of Gehennom. The Wizard seemed to show up an
awful lot, but I had two wands of death and the PYEC, so there was no
real danger. Humorously, I misidentified a ring of teleport control as
free action. So throughout the end of the game I was under the
impression that I had free action when I didn't. :)

So onto the Planes. Earth, as usual, was painfully easy. Even moreso
because the portal was about twenty steps away. Air was, ahem, tricky.
I didn't have any permanent source of levitation; I kept hoping I
would run into a ring and not have to burn a wish for it. But I gave
in and wished up =oLev. I wandered around for a little while because
the Orb stopped working (anselmus later told me, on Fire, that the
message I was getting indicated it was out of charges -- oops).

Made it to Fire, still kept trying with the Orb. I ended up running
around a lot, getting things to chase me, hoping one of the monsters
would trip onto the portal. No dice. An Archon eventually showed up
and made things hellish. He summoned quite a bit, I ended up spending
my last wish on a wand of teleportation just to get him out of my
hair.

Somehow I made it to Water. Unfortunately my PYEC wouldn't recharge my
Orb so I stumbled around for a good five minutes. But I made it to
Astral. Astral was pretty simple (watch how I do Astral on all of my
ascensions on AstralTV at telnet noway.ratry.ru port 37331 and you'll
see.. it's basically tele + jump + conflict). It did start off kind of
rough with a master lich doing a bit of summoning.

So that's all. I'm pretty proud of this one. :)

